  "prefLabel": "Nur 404.10 Circumstances Prohibiting the Performance by an LNA of Tasks Involving Medication Administration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 404.10 Circumstances Prohibiting the Performance by an LNA of Tasks Involving Medication Administration. An MNA shall not perform a task involving the administration of medication if:\n\n(a) The task requires the determination of the client's need for the medication, the calculation of the dosage of the medication or the conversion of dosage;\n\n(b) The delegating nurse is unavailable to monitor the progress of the client and the effect on the client of the medication; or\n\n(c) The client is not stable or has changing nursing needs.\n\nSource. #8873, eff 4-24-07; ss by #10299, eff 3-22-13; ss by #10571, eff 4-17-14; renumbered by #10953 (from Nur 404.09)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nur100-800.html"
